        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Checking people in</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">22</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>At the door, the same Point of Sale that sells tickets checks in the people who bought them beforehand. Scan a ticket on the register screen (scanner or camera) and it's checked in: green for checked in, amber if they're already in (with the time), red for a ticket for another day, cancelled, unconfirmed, or an event that's over.</p><p><span class="oe-path">⋮ Actions › Check In</span> opens the door list: today's events with how many are in, a search by name, email, phone or ticket number, and a <strong>Check in</strong> button for each person.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/performers_elearning_events/static/img/door_list.png" alt="The Check In list in the Point of Sale" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>the door list, one of four in.</p></div><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-ticket" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Selling at the door</span><p>Tickets sold at the door are an ordinary Point of Sale sale: pick the event, the ticket and the guest's details.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
